popActivity: never leave the focus in the popped activity

The activity is deleted after its hide animation. With nothing saved on the
focus stack when it opened, or a saved view hidden meanwhile, the focus
stayed on one of its views, and the next giveFocus() called onFocusLost()
on deleted memory (AnkiNX crashed on opening with automatic sync on).

--- a/library/lib/core/application.cpp	2026-10-22 23:10:52.014652200 -0300
+++ b/library/lib/core/application.cpp	2026-10-22 23:10:52.530751800 -0300
@@ -944,6 +944,18 @@
         Application::focusStack.pop_back();
     }
 
+    // Never leave the focus in the activity being popped: it is deleted after
+    // its animation, and the next focus change would use the deleted view.
+    // That happens when no focus was saved as it opened, or when the saved
+    // view can't take the focus any more (hidden meanwhile).
+    if (Application::currentFocus && Application::currentFocus->getParentActivity() == last)
+    {
+        if (toShow)
+            Application::giveFocus(toShow->getContentView());
+        if (Application::currentFocus && Application::currentFocus->getParentActivity() == last)
+            Application::currentFocus = nullptr;
+    }
+
     // Hide animation (and show previous activity, if any)
     last->hide([last, cb, free]()
         {
